# Custom Checkstyle Property Expansion Definitions

You can define custom [property expansion definitions](https://checkstyle.org/config.html#Properties) for the Checker.

Checkstyle uses the property expansion mechanism to inject specific values into a pre-defined Checker configuration.
Property expansion alone is not enough to customize the checks that Checkstyle performs.

Example: `checkstyle.xml` - This configuration checks the package name in use.
It makes sure that the package name conforms to the desired scheme.
It also lets the Checker users specify their own projectname.

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" ?>

<!DOCTYPE module PUBLIC
  "-//Checkstyle//DTD Checkstyle Configuration 1.2//EN"
  "https://checkstyle.org/dtds/configuration_1_2.dtd">

<module name="Checker">
  <module name="TreeWalker">
    <module name="PackageName">
      <property name="format"
         value="com\.example\.$\{projectname\}(\.[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]+)*$"/>
    </module>
  </module>
</module>
```

Example: `pom.xml` - This configuration specifies the `projectname` property expansion.
Checkstyle uses it when it encounters the variable in the Checker configuration above.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <configLocation>checkstyle.xml</configLocation>
          <propertyExpansion>
            projectname=whizbang
            anotherProperty=bazinga
          </propertyExpansion>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

You can also provide the property expansion information from a location with the `propertiesLocation` parameter as shown below.
The parameter can point to a URL, a file, or a build classpath resource.

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <configLocation>checkstyle.xml</configLocation>
          <propertiesLocation>${basedir}/checkstyle.properties</propertiesLocation>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```
